{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>Day, and to you they shall come</b> — to you. Every nation dwells from Assyria to the river Euprat. And Rabbi Yeshuah said: <i>and sea of waters</i> — that from the west of the land of Israel it shall be rebuilt, from the direction of the sea and such-and-such mountain which was entirely settled, like a mountain. And in my opinion: for the word <i>and to the river</i> draws after it <i>and to the sea of waters and mountain</i> and <i>to the mountain</i>, and behold <i>sea of waters</i> is like <i>the former sea</i> and <i>the latter sea</i>, and likewise <i>the southern mountain</i> to <i>the northern</i>."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The lemma and commentary are textually difficult; rendered hyper-literally. The verse citation appears fragmentary and the syntax of Rabbi Yeshuah's interpretation is obscure in the Hebrew; 'it shall be rebuilt' reads the verb שב as a form of שוב in the sense of restoration, though the form is unusual."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:14:18.736340879Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}